WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.601 --> 00:00:05.407
- On this episode, the
legend Fat Joe stops by.

00:00:05.407 --> 00:00:09.232
- [Gary] The #AskGaryVee Show.

00:00:11.712 --> 00:00:13.806
- Hey everybody, 
this is Gary Vay-ner-chuk

00:00:13.806 --> 00:00:18.785
and this is episode 218 of 
The #AskGaryVee Show.

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:22.256
And if you're a Jersey boy, east
coast if you love music you're

00:00:22.256 --> 00:00:26.126
as happy as I am right now
because I have a legend with me

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:27.861
Fat Joe, my man.
- Sup my brother?

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:30.330
- Why don't you tell the Vayner
Nation for the one person who's

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:33.467
watching this in who knows where
in the world that doesn't know

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:34.801
who you are, why don't you spend

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.637
a minute to say hello to
the Vayner Nation.

00:00:36.637 --> 00:00:37.838
- How's it going my brothers?

00:00:37.838 --> 00:00:41.802
My name is Fat Joe originally
from the Bronx, New York

00:00:41.802 --> 00:00:44.945
reside in Miami for 
the last 14 years.

00:00:44.945 --> 00:00:48.971
- [Gary] The weather?
- Amazing in Miami.

00:00:50.371 --> 00:00:53.120
Originally a member of the
Diggin' In The Crates crew

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:57.691
that's Lord Finesse, Showbiz,
happy birthday Lord Finesse.

00:00:57.691 --> 00:01:02.081
Showbiz and A.G., 
Diamond D, O.C.,

00:01:02.081 --> 00:01:04.131
Big L rest in peace.

00:01:04.131 --> 00:01:08.235
Then the leading founder and
president of Terror Squad rest

00:01:08.235 --> 00:01:12.560
in peace Big Pun, Remy Ma,

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:16.240
DJ Khaled the list goes on and on,

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:19.947
and whatever, Fat Joe.

00:01:19.947 --> 00:01:23.483
- Listen, I'm sure everybody
knows and if they don't

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:24.985
that's their mistake.

00:01:24.985 --> 00:01:26.787
Tell me what's on
your mind these days?

00:01:26.787 --> 00:01:28.121
A lot of people that
are watching right now

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:31.625
entrepreneurs, marketers and
business people, the kind of

00:01:31.625 --> 00:01:33.169
people you would enjoy.

00:01:33.169 --> 00:01:36.997
I was born in Russia came up
baseball cards, lemonade stand,

00:01:36.997 --> 00:01:39.967
a lot of people watch this
hustling, making this happen.

00:01:39.967 --> 00:01:41.301
What's going on in
your business world?

00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:42.169
What are you excited about?

00:01:42.169 --> 00:01:45.605
Obviously Khaled had this
phenomenal situation in the last

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.140
year with Snapchat.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.142
Obviously you've
been out and about.

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:53.347
- Well, you know I am president
of urban and Latino division a

00:01:53.347 --> 00:01:55.911
company called
MarketAmericaShop.com.

00:01:55.911 --> 00:01:57.409
- Yep.

00:01:57.409 --> 00:01:59.963
- We teach people how to be
entrepreneurs and teach them the

00:01:59.963 --> 00:02:02.628
importance of residual income.
- Yes.

00:02:02.628 --> 00:02:06.053
- Working one time in your 
life and always getting

00:02:06.053 --> 00:02:08.034
paid for it forever.

00:02:08.034 --> 00:02:11.793
So I work with my Latinos and
my Black people in this business

00:02:11.793 --> 00:02:16.549
but the business has been around
for 24 years and and Asians and

00:02:16.549 --> 00:02:20.407
white people you know have
made the three and half billion

00:02:20.407 --> 00:02:22.442
dollars doing this
business right here.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:25.712
So I'm teaching the Latinos and
the Black people how to do this.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:29.916
We sell vitamins, we sell make
up, all those cosmetics so I've

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:33.387
been doing that for the last
two years as well as I've always

00:02:33.387 --> 00:02:36.123
been doing my music.
- Always.

00:02:36.123 --> 00:02:37.991
- My main hustle is my music.

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:40.193
I've been doing
that since day one.

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:41.228
- When did music hit your life?

00:02:41.228 --> 00:02:43.263
Literally out the womb?
When you are three?

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:45.932
- Well I loved
music since day one.

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:50.804
But growing up in the Bronx
emulating my brother

00:02:50.804 --> 00:02:53.373
you know what I'm saying looking
outside my window is pretty much

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:57.344
where hip hop music was created.
- Of course.

00:02:57.344 --> 00:03:02.182
- We had what we used to
call jams, block parties right

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:03.683
outside my window.

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:06.553
So me being four or five years
old I used to see them come

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:10.557
outside, bring the turntables
and we used to go out there and

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:12.692
listen to the music and then 
I just fell in love with

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:15.562
hip hop, breakdancing and
graffiti.

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:18.799
I got into so much trouble
writing graffiti on trains.

00:03:18.799 --> 00:03:23.800
I got thrown out of maybe
six, seven junior high schools

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.891
writing graffitis.

00:03:26.891 --> 00:03:29.776
And then I got into rapping
and battle rapping everybody.

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:33.747
I always say I was the original
Eminem 'cause I used to battle a

00:03:33.747 --> 00:03:36.917
whole bunch of Black kids but 
I had a blonde hair and

00:03:36.917 --> 00:03:40.420
green eyes and I was 
kicking that gangster shit.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:43.790
And they was looking out like 
I was fucking crazy every time.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.392
- Yep. You got a reputation.

00:03:45.392 --> 00:03:46.493
- Here we are.
- Yep.

00:03:46.493 --> 00:03:50.536
So actually my own, now I'm
being selfish, I'm sorry,

00:03:50.536 --> 00:03:52.461
I'm just taking full advantage.

00:03:52.461 --> 00:03:55.654
What's your point of view on
the current state of hip hop?

00:03:55.654 --> 00:03:58.538
What are you seeing out there 
what are your thoughts on some

00:03:58.538 --> 00:04:00.707
of the people that are coming up?
What people listen to?

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:02.198
- I love J Cole.
- Yep.

00:04:02.198 --> 00:04:04.675
- I'm a huge J Cole fan.

00:04:04.675 --> 00:04:08.430
I love his
freedom of expression.

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:12.757
Pusha T's my favorite album.

00:04:13.447 --> 00:04:16.374
I love Kanye West's new album.

00:04:17.914 --> 00:04:21.589
I love music, man, and
everything is gotta evolve.

00:04:21.589 --> 00:04:23.156
- That's right.
- You know what I'm saying?

00:04:23.156 --> 00:04:26.211
I love our era that I
came out of in the 90s.

00:04:26.211 --> 00:04:26.878
- Yep.

00:04:26.878 --> 00:04:30.743
- I also think the era before
ours, the LL Cool J,

00:04:30.743 --> 00:04:34.829
Public Enemy, Heavy D, 
KRS One was better than ours.

00:04:34.829 --> 00:04:35.666
- Sure.

00:04:35.666 --> 00:04:38.784
You grew up with it, right?
- Yeah, I grew up with it.

00:04:38.784 --> 00:04:40.832
- You feel like a lot of the
legends, the people have been

00:04:40.832 --> 00:04:43.617
through it like yourself,
sometimes too often are quick to

00:04:43.617 --> 00:04:48.221
downplay seven years ago the
South or new guys that come up?

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:50.457
Do you feel like
there's too much of that?

00:04:50.457 --> 00:04:51.792
Like, people are trying to
push against it because

00:04:51.792 --> 00:04:52.592
it's not theirs?

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:56.196
- Yeah, I believe, 
I believe it needs to evolve.

00:04:56.196 --> 00:04:56.863
- That's right.

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:58.198
- I just believe--
- 'Cause it will, right?

00:04:58.198 --> 00:04:59.533
You can accept it--

00:04:59.533 --> 00:05:02.536
- You can go with
it or it leaves you.

00:05:02.536 --> 00:05:03.703
- Exactly. Exactly.

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:06.873
- And I don't want to sound
like the grouchy old rapper.

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:07.908
- Right. In my day.

00:05:07.908 --> 00:05:09.743
- Yeah, in my day was like this.

00:05:09.743 --> 00:05:12.679
We just gotta embrace the youth.
You know?

00:05:12.679 --> 00:05:14.191
- You ready to
answer some questions?

00:05:14.191 --> 00:05:15.022
- Absolutely.

00:05:15.022 --> 00:05:16.449
- India?
- Ready.

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:18.385
- You ready to ask some questions?
- I am.

00:05:18.385 --> 00:05:20.787
- India, did you think that you
have a day in your career where

00:05:20.787 --> 00:05:22.722
you were going to
ask Fat Joe questions?

00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:24.758
Was this something that when you
thought as a little girl growing

00:05:24.758 --> 00:05:26.760
up in San Francisco.
- No.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:28.510
- Yeah. Let's fire away.
- Cool.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:29.596
First one's from Clayton.

00:05:29.596 --> 00:05:32.499
- Oh video. Clayton. Alright.

00:05:32.499 --> 00:05:35.235
- Hey Fat Joe,
welcome to the show.

00:05:36.265 --> 00:05:39.306
The question I have is you 
did that song with Ashanti

00:05:40.176 --> 00:05:42.976
a while ago. I think it's
called "What's Love".

00:05:42.976 --> 00:05:45.811
How do artists ever hook up and

00:05:45.811 --> 00:05:48.481
how do they get to collaborate

00:05:48.481 --> 00:05:49.216
with each other?

00:05:49.216 --> 00:05:53.620
Is there somebody like producers
that brings that or agent,

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:55.361
how does that happen?

00:05:55.361 --> 00:05:58.258
- How do collabo's happen?
Take it away.

00:05:58.258 --> 00:06:02.062
- A lot of times with me when
I make music I hear a certain

00:06:02.062 --> 00:06:05.265
artist on it and I reach out 
and I hope they want to

00:06:05.265 --> 00:06:06.633
work with me.
- Like flat-out?

00:06:06.633 --> 00:06:09.469
You got it in your head and
you're like this would be

00:06:09.469 --> 00:06:10.104
perfect for this person?

00:06:10.104 --> 00:06:11.390
- Let's skip that.
- Go ahead.

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:15.247
- Let's just say Cool &amp;amp; Dre,

00:06:15.247 --> 00:06:17.377
Scott Storch may get it popping

00:06:17.377 --> 00:06:19.813
and I immediately
heard Nelly on there.

00:06:19.813 --> 00:06:24.651
So we reached out and Cool &amp;amp; Dre
wrote the hook and I reached out

00:06:24.651 --> 00:06:25.619
to Nelly and I was like,

00:06:25.619 --> 00:06:27.687
"Nelly, do you want to do 
this hook over for me,"

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:28.898
and he said yes.

00:06:28.898 --> 00:06:31.149
We heard him on the song.

00:06:31.149 --> 00:06:34.030
"Make It Rain" I wrote the hook
to "Make It Rain" and I heard

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:37.445
Lil Wayne on it because it was a
South song and I was like,

00:06:37.445 --> 00:06:40.000
"Yo, Wayne can you do this
over," he did it.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.303
You hear certain artist that you
want to collaborate with on the

00:06:43.303 --> 00:06:44.571
songs and you hope sometimes.

00:06:44.571 --> 00:06:47.474
- Have you ever been devastated
when you've really wanted it?

00:06:47.474 --> 00:06:50.944
- Not devastated but I've been
chasing Future on this album and

00:06:50.944 --> 00:06:54.086
he's been acting
real Hollywood with me.

00:06:54.086 --> 00:06:56.283
Acting like he don't
want to do this song.

00:06:56.283 --> 00:06:58.218
- Uh-huh.
- Got to be honest with you.

00:06:58.218 --> 00:06:59.552
- Playing hard to get you think?

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:01.354
- Yeah, hard to get
sometimes it's like that.

00:07:01.354 --> 00:07:02.422
You know?
- Of course.

00:07:02.422 --> 00:07:04.591
Let me play it in for
everybody who's watching.

00:07:04.591 --> 00:07:06.593
Same thing in business, a lot of
people always ask me how do you

00:07:06.593 --> 00:07:08.662
get an angel deals when you
invest in the people when you

00:07:08.662 --> 00:07:10.697
are doing these things?
It comes in all forms.

00:07:10.697 --> 00:07:14.034
Sometimes it comes to you,
sometimes reach out but I love,

00:07:14.034 --> 00:07:16.336
I was curious how you
were going to answer it.

00:07:16.336 --> 00:07:20.240
I think sometimes people try to
big up too much and I have too

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:23.143
much pride and they don't want
to reach out. When you want

00:07:23.143 --> 00:07:24.778
something you have to
go out and grab it.

00:07:24.778 --> 00:07:28.315
I love instead of you saying oh
sometimes it comes to me or this

00:07:28.315 --> 00:07:30.583
and that you said look I hear
somebody I wanted,

00:07:30.583 --> 00:07:31.251
I'll reach out.

00:07:31.251 --> 00:07:34.154
Sometimes they say yes,
sometimes they say no.

00:07:34.154 --> 00:07:36.623
Way too many people
watching right now, you know how

00:07:36.623 --> 00:07:38.958
successful this
man is in his genre?

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:41.594
You know how many of you are
too proud to reach out to do

00:07:41.594 --> 00:07:44.487
something with somebody and you
haven't made shit happen yet.

00:07:45.347 --> 00:07:48.756
- Nah, that's not how it works.
- No, it is not.

00:07:48.756 --> 00:07:50.140
- That's not how it works.

00:07:50.140 --> 00:07:52.684
- I think one thing and I'll use
this moment I've been wanting to

00:07:52.684 --> 00:07:56.123
say this to really win you
have to equally pull

00:07:56.123 --> 00:07:58.798
at ego and humility.

00:07:59.978 --> 00:08:00.608
What do you think?

00:08:00.608 --> 00:08:02.796
- What I have done, 
what I've done

00:08:04.646 --> 00:08:06.886
the new Fat Joe--

00:08:06.886 --> 00:08:09.943
- And when did the new Fat
Joe come out in your world?

00:08:09.943 --> 00:08:13.159
- Maybe this year.
- Okay.

00:08:13.159 --> 00:08:14.727
- Let's just say
it all the way up.

00:08:14.727 --> 00:08:16.665
- Okay. Yep.

00:08:16.665 --> 00:08:22.068
- I've had riffs and not
everything was so good between

00:08:22.068 --> 00:08:23.937
me and Jay-Z in the past.
- [Gary] Yep. Yep.

00:08:23.937 --> 00:08:26.172
- I reached out to him--
- [Gary] Be the bigger man.

00:08:26.172 --> 00:08:29.409
- Yes and collaborated
and we did the remix.

00:08:31.079 --> 00:08:32.145
- [Gary] That was big
news in that world.

00:08:32.145 --> 00:08:33.746
That was big news.

00:08:33.746 --> 00:08:37.484
- I did not see eye to
eye with Daddy Yankee.

00:08:37.484 --> 00:08:40.253
I got him on the Spanish remix.
- [Gary] Mhmmm.

00:08:40.253 --> 00:08:43.739
- Me and 50 Cent made peace

00:08:43.739 --> 00:08:45.859
and now we performed together not

00:08:45.859 --> 00:08:48.561
too long ago.
I laid down.

00:08:48.561 --> 00:08:49.685
- [Gary] Are you enjoying this?

00:08:49.685 --> 00:08:53.066
- I'm enjoying it because you
eliminate all the barriers.

00:08:53.066 --> 00:08:54.801
- That's right.
- You know what I'm saying?

00:08:54.801 --> 00:08:56.936
All the enemies and
all the people--

00:08:56.936 --> 00:08:59.305
- When did this happen?
January 1 thing for you?

00:08:59.305 --> 00:08:59.973
Was it a long time?

00:08:59.973 --> 00:09:02.041
- It wasn't January 1.
It was just me.

00:09:02.041 --> 00:09:04.644
I tried all the wars--
- Right.

00:09:04.644 --> 00:09:06.980
- And then I just said to
myself, you know what I'm going

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:09.582
to eliminate all obstacles.

00:09:09.582 --> 00:09:14.741
And I'm going to try to say 
put all ego and pride aside

00:09:14.741 --> 00:09:18.224
and let me just try 
the non-ego route.

00:09:18.224 --> 00:09:22.429
Let me try working with
everybody and see how this

00:09:22.429 --> 00:09:25.178
workin' and so far we're
platinum on the single,

00:09:25.178 --> 00:09:27.838
go on to double platinum,
tours opening up--

00:09:27.838 --> 00:09:29.769
- Go figure.
Go figure.

00:09:30.849 --> 00:09:33.565
Go with positivity
and imagine that.

00:09:33.565 --> 00:09:37.155
- It's a magical miracle
pill that seems to be working.

00:09:37.155 --> 00:09:39.198
- Yeah, it happens.
I'm glad you went there.

00:09:39.198 --> 00:09:41.681
It's been a theme of mine
over my whole life but

00:09:41.681 --> 00:09:43.049
I've been really...

00:09:43.049 --> 00:09:44.851
With all the shit that's 
going on in the world,

00:09:46.031 --> 00:09:47.754
if you can't go half glass full.

00:09:47.754 --> 00:09:51.024
If you can't be the person of
change and drive positivity and

00:09:51.024 --> 00:09:53.370
optimism I just
think it is a mistake.

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:54.335
India.
- Mhmmm.

00:09:54.335 --> 00:09:56.286
- [India] This is from Craig.
- Craig.

00:09:56.286 --> 00:09:58.331
- [Voiceover] Craig asked, 
"What do you think people like

00:09:58.331 --> 00:10:00.664
"Chance the Rapper releasing a
lot of his music for free as a

00:10:00.664 --> 00:10:02.469
"marketing strategy?"

00:10:02.469 --> 00:10:04.571
- What do you think Chance the
Rapper, people like

00:10:04.571 --> 00:10:06.639
Chance the Rapper, what do you
think about Chance's music?

00:10:06.639 --> 00:10:10.223
- I love Chance the Rapper.
- I'm obsessed.

00:10:10.223 --> 00:10:12.011
(mumbled singing)

00:10:15.131 --> 00:10:17.217
What do you think about 
people like Chance

00:10:17.217 --> 00:10:19.886
and others that are putting
out a lot of mixtapes, a lot of

00:10:19.886 --> 00:10:22.956
product for free as a 
marketing play or

00:10:22.956 --> 00:10:24.157
whatever the strategy may be?

00:10:24.157 --> 00:10:24.958
- I love it. I love it.

00:10:24.958 --> 00:10:29.929
I think you keep the relevancy
and you keep the fans engaged.

00:10:31.779 --> 00:10:34.634
I love it.
I think it's a hustle.

00:10:34.634 --> 00:10:38.271
It shows that you dedicated to
the art and at the end of the

00:10:38.271 --> 00:10:43.251
day the art wasn't meant 
to be materialism and

00:10:43.251 --> 00:10:44.580
everything is a dollar.

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:46.946
It's about giving back
to your fans anyway.

00:10:46.946 --> 00:10:49.949
- I think the one thing that a
lot of you are watching know is

00:10:49.949 --> 00:10:53.987
I don't have the $500
e-books and the $7,000 courses.

00:10:53.987 --> 00:10:55.288
I do the shows for free.

00:10:55.288 --> 00:10:57.824
I pump out content
at scale for free.

00:10:57.824 --> 00:11:00.393
Thousands of you email me 
every single month,

00:11:00.393 --> 00:11:01.327
"You should charge for this.

00:11:01.327 --> 00:11:03.563
"This is better than the
shit I'm paying more for."

00:11:03.563 --> 00:11:07.767
It plays into that same thesis
which is yes but that's why so

00:11:07.767 --> 00:11:09.702
many more of you follow me.

00:11:09.702 --> 00:11:12.038
- You get engaged. Yes.
- Of course.

00:11:12.038 --> 00:11:15.441
Either you're running a marathon
or you're running a sprint.

00:11:15.441 --> 00:11:17.677
Figure out what you are doing.
- Exactly.

00:11:17.677 --> 00:11:20.474
- India.
- [India] Next one from OTFN.

00:11:20.474 --> 00:11:23.650
- [Voiceover] OTWHouston asked,
"What is the most important or

00:11:23.650 --> 00:11:26.653
"best aspect of a live
music event or experience?"

00:11:26.653 --> 00:11:28.421
- I can't answer that.

00:11:28.421 --> 00:11:31.324
- The most important aspect?
- This is you.

